#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write the vision boards into this repository.

This one file carries the eight vision boards the CA-29 to CA-54 series is
built against (Home, OpenBuilds, Builds Table, Maps and Classification,
Library, Composer Add from Library, Drafts): each board's design source, the
board rendered to standalone HTML, a picture of it, and the index the compare
harness reads. Running it writes them under <repo root>/design/: 26 files,
about 2.1 MB.

    python3 design/vision-kit.py          # write the boards
    python3 design/vision-kit.py --check  # verify what is on disk, write nothing

Safe to re-run: it overwrites these files with the same bytes and touches
nothing else. No dependencies beyond the standard library.

What it writes:

    design/reference/vision/index.json           the boards: file, kind, theme, page,
                                                 width, height, title, devPage, source, screen
    design/reference/vision/dusk/<board>.html    standalone HTML, 1440 wide, Dusk. Values exact.
    design/reference/vision/source/<Board>.dc.html  the design canvas sources, with their
                                                 sample data in the text/x-dc script
    design/screens/vision/<board>.png            a picture of each board, for looking at
    design/scripts/render-vision-board.mjs       the renderer that made the HTML from a source

The standalone HTML carries no script. It was rendered from the canvas
sources with the canvas's NEW notes and Home's legend turned off, the Google
Fonts links replaced by the repo's own Geist and Geist Mono in
design/reference/fonts/ (which must exist, as build-kit.py writes it), and
every sample value filled in. Each board renders in Chromium at 1440 wide with
no errors and no failed request, at the height in index.json.

To refresh a board after the canvas changes, put the new source in
design/reference/vision/source/ and run, from the repo root:

    node design/scripts/render-vision-board.mjs \
      design/reference/vision/source/<Board>.dc.html design/reference/vision/dusk/<board>.html

then measure its height at 1440 wide, update index.json and retake the picture.

Every name, handle, number, date and sentence in a board is sample content.
Source: the "buildgallery Home vision" design canvas, version 1792945557-56d9,
read on 25 October 2026.
"""
